<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<usx version="2.0">
  <book code="RUT" style="id">Ruthi</book>
  <para style="h">Ruthi</para>
  <para style="toc1">Ruthi</para>
  <para style="toc2">Ruthi</para>
  <para style="mt">Ruthi</para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Rorêltuten ro an rêl lai khân, Israel ramah ṭâm a tla a. Judai ram Bethlehem khuaa mi pakhat chu a nupui leh a fapa pahnih nên Moab ramah ṭâm tlân tûrin an kal a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Chu mi hming chu Elimeleka a ni a, a nupui hming chu Naomi a ni; an fate hming chu Mahlona leh Kiliona a ni. Judai ram Bethlehem khuaa Efrata mi an ni. Moab ramah chuan an kal a, chutah chuan an awm ta reng a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Naomi pasal Elimeleka chu a thi a; tichuan, Naomi chu a fapa pahnihte nên chauh an awm ta a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />A fate chuan Moab mi nupuiah an nei a, pakhat hming chu Orpi a ni a, a dang hming chu Ruthi a ni. Chuta kum sâwm lai an awm hnu chuan
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Mahlona leh Kiliona chu an thi ve leh ta a, chu nu chu a pasal leh a fapate chuan an thihsan ve leh ta a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Tin, Lalpa chuan a mite a ṭanpui a, ei tûr a pe tih Moab ram aṭang chuan an lo hria a, a mote nên chuan Moab ram ata haw tûrin an insiam ta a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />A mo pahnih nên chuan an awmna hmun chhuahsanin Judai ram an pan ta a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Nakinah chuan Naomi chuan a mo pahnihte hnênah chuan, “In nute in lamah haw ve ve zâwk rawh u, ka chungah leh in pasal thi tate chunga khawngaihna in lantîr ang khân, Lalpa chuan khawngaih che u rawh se.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Lalpan in pahnihin thlamuang taka pasal te hmua in awm theih nân khawngaih che u rawh se,” a ti a. Anni chu a fâwp a, râwl chhuah meuhvin an ṭap ta a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />A mote chuan, “Kan haw lo vang, i mite hnêna i kal tûr hi kan zui ve zâwk ang che,” an ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Naomi chuan, “Ka fanute u, haw zâwk rawh u. Engah nge ka hnênah chuan in kal ve kher ang? In pasal tûr fapa ka nei leh thei dâwn em ni?
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Ka fanute u, in in lamah haw leh rawh u. Pasal han nei tûrin ka upa lutuk tawh si a, ‘ka bei a la sei reng e,’ tiin zâninah pawh hian pasal neiin fapa te pawh han nei tehrêng ila,
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />an puitlin thlengin in nghâk dâwn em ni ang? Pasal lovin in awm reng dâwn em ni? Ni lul lo ve, ka fanute u, nangmahni avâng hian ka rilru a na êm êm a ni, Lalpa kut ka tuar ta si a,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Chu veleh râwl chhuah meuhvin an ṭap leh ta a, Orpi chuan a pi chu a fâwp a, a kîrsan ta a. Ruthi erawh chuan a vuan tlat a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Naomi chuan, “En teh, i mopui pawh a chite leh a pathian hnênah a hâwn leh tâk saw, i mopui saw zui haw ve rawh,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Ruthi erawh chuan, “Nangmah ṭhen tûr leh kîrsan tûr che chuan min thlêm lo hrâm rawh; i kalna apiangah ka kal ang a, i riahna apiangah ka riak ang; i chite chu ka chite an ni ang a, i Pathian chu ka Pathian a ni ang.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />I thihnaah ka thi ang a, chutah chuan min phûm ve mai rawh se. Nang leh kei hi thihna chauh lo chuan thil dangin min ṭhen dâwn ai chuan Lalpan eng ang pawhin; a duh duhin min ti rawh se,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />A hnêna kal ve a tum tlat tih a hriatin Naomi chuan a ngawihsan ta a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Tichuan, Bethlehem thlengin an kal dûn ta a. Bethlehem an han thlen chuan a khuain an phu ta mur mur a, nuho chuan, “Hei Naomi kha a ni maw?” an ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Naomi chuan an hnênah, “Naomi min ti tawh suh u, Marai min ti zâwk rawh u. Engkimtitheia chuan na takin min thunun ta si a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Kokim takin kan kal chhuak a, Lalpa chuan kutbêngin min hruai hâwng leh ta a nih hi. Engati nge, Naomi min la tih cheu le, Lalpa chuan min thunun a, Engkimtitheia chuan ka chungah chhiatna a thlentîr ta si a,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Naomi chu a monu Moab mi nên Moab ram aṭangin an lo kîr a, barli seng ṭan tirh laiin Bethlehem khua chu an lo thleng a ni.
  </para>
  <chapter number="2" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Naomi chuan a pasal Elimeleka laichîn, a hming Boaza, mi neinung tak chhûng hnai a nei a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Moab mi Ruthi chuan Naomi hnênah, “Ka va feh ang a, buhṭo ka va zawng ang e, min lo khawngaih thei an lo awm mahna,” a ti a. Naomi chuan, “Kal ta che, ka fanu,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Tichuan, a kal ta a, buhsengtute buh lâk hmaih chu a va zawng a. Elimeleka laichîn Boaza lovah a va kal fuh hlauh va.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Boaza pawh Bethlehem aṭang chuan a lo thleng ve a, buhsengtute hnênah chuan, “ Lalpa in hnênah awm rawh se,” a ti a. Anni chuan, “ Lalpa chuan malsâwm che rawh se,” tiin an lo chhâng a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Boaza chuan a chhiahhlawh, buhseng hotu hnênah chuan, “Hei, khawi lam hmeichhia nge ni le?” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />A chhiahhlawh, buhseng hotu chuan, “He mi hi Moab hmeichhia, Naomi ruala Moab ram aṭanga lo kal kha a ni.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />‘Buhsengtute buhphal khâwm hmaih ka zawng ang e,’ tiin min dîl a; rei lo tê bûka a han châwl zawk tih loh chu zîng aṭangin tûn thlengin rim takin a thawk reng a nih hi,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Boaza chuan Ruthi hnênah chuan, “Ka fanu, ka hrilh a che. Lo dangah buhṭo zawng suh la, heta ta hi kal sawn suh ang che. Chhiahhlawh nulate hnênah hian awm ve reng la;
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />khawi lamah nge buh an seng en thlithlai la, nulate hi zui zêl ang che. Tlangvâlte pawh eng mah tih lo tûr chein thu ka pe a; i tui a hâl chângin tuibêla tlangvâlte tui chawi sa hi i in ṭhîn dâwn nia,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Tichuan, ani chu hmai lei siin a kûn a, “Kei hnam dang mi lehnghâl min hre duh a, heti taka min khawngaih hi engtizia nge ni le?” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Boaza chuan heti hian a chhâng a, “I pasal thih a chin tûn thlengin i pi chunga i thil tih zawng zawng miin min hrilh a; i nu te, i pa te, i pianna ram te kalsana, i la hriat loh mite zînga chêng tûra i lo kal dân te pawh min hrilh a ni.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Lalpa chuan i thiltih man rûl che sela; Lalpa , Israel-te Pathian, inhumhim nâna a thlahnuai i rawn chuha chuan i ṭhat man pe ṭeuh che rawh se,” tiin.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Ani chuan, “Ka pu, nangin min khawngaih avângin ka thla a muang ta. I chhiahhlawh nulate zînga mi ni lo mah ila, i chhiahhlawhnu hi ṭha takin i be ta si a,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Chawfâk a lo hun chuan Boaza chuan a hnênah, “Hetah lo kal la, chhang te hi ei ve la, chhang hi uain thûrah te han chiah ve rawh khai,” a ti a. Tichuan, buhsengtute kiangah chuan a ṭhu ve a, chhangpêr a lo pe a, puar taka a ei hnuin a la ei bâng ta cheu va.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Buhṭo chu a han zawng leh a, Boaza chuan tlangvâlte hnênah chuan, “Buh ahna zînga mi pawh la sela, hau suh ang che u.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />A têl aṭangin buhvuite phawichhuahsak ula, a chhar tûrin hnutchhiah ang che u, hau rêng rêng suh u,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Lovah chuan tlai thlengin buhṭo chu a zawng a, a zawn sa chu a vua a, efa khat lai a ni.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />A phur a, khuaah a hâwnpui ta a, a pi chuan a buhṭo lâk chu a lo hmu a, Ruthi chuan an chhang ei bâng chu a phawrh a, ani chu a pe a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />A pi chuan a hnênah, “Vawiinah khawi lama buhṭo nge i zawn a, tu lovah nge i va thawh le? A lo khawngaihtu che chu malsâwmin awm rawh se,” a ti a. Ruthi chuan a pi hnênah chuan a va thawhna chu hetiang hian a hrilh a: “Vawiina ka va thawhna pa chu a hming Boaza a ni,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Naomi chuan a monu hnênah chuan, “ Lalpa , mi nung leh mitthi chunga a khawngaih bâng chuang ngai lova chuan ani chu malsâwm rawh se, chu mi chu kan chipûi, kan laichîn hnai tak a ni asin,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Moab mi Ruthi chuan, “ ‘Buh hi an seng zawh thlengin hnathawktute zîngah hian thawk ang che’ min ti nghe nghe asin,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Naomi chuan a monu Ruthi hnênah chuan, “A ṭhat chu, a hnathawk nulate zîngah hlîr thawk la, lo dangah zawng an khawih buai palh ang che,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Tichuan, Ruthi chu Boaza nula chhawrte zîngah chuan barli leh huit seng zawh thlengin buhṭo zawng chuan a awm a, a pi hnênah chuan a awm ta reng a.
  </para>
  <chapter number="3" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Chumi hnu chuan a pi Naomi chuan a hnênah, “Ka fanu, ngaihngam taka i khawsak theihna tûr ka ngaihtuahsak ang che.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />A chhiahhlawh nulate nêna hna i va thawhna pa kha kan laichîn bul Boaza a ni. Ngai teh, zânin hi hruihah barli a zah fai zân a ni a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Inbual la, rimtui te inchulh la, i thawmhnaw ṭha ber inbelin hruihah chuan zu kal rawh. Amaherawhchu, a eia a in zawh hma chuan a hnênah inlan suh ang che.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />A mut hunah a mutna chhinchhiah la, a ke chu hlim la, mu ve ang che. Tichuan, i tih tûr chu a lo hrilh mai ang che,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Ruthi chuan, “I sawi ang chuan ka ti ang e,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Tichuan, hruih lamah chuan a chhuk a, a pi hrilh ang chuan a ti ta a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />A eia a in zawh hnu chuan Boaza chu hlim takin buh vûm sirah chuan a mu ta a. Nakinah chuan Ruthi chu dîm têin a va kal a, a ke chu a hlîm a, a mu ve ta a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Zanlaiah chuan Boaza chu a lo ṭhangharh a, a han hawi a, a ke bula hmeichhe lo mu reng chu a hmu ta a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />“Tu nge i nih?” a ti a. Ani chuan, “I chhiahhlawhnu Ruthi ka ni. Kan laichîn bul i ni bawk a, i puan kha mi han zâwn teh,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Ani chuan, “ Lalpa chuan malsâwm che rawh se; tlangvâl rethei emaw, hausa emaw i zui mai mai loh dânah hian, tûnhma ai mahin tûnah hian i chhûngte laka i rinawmzia i tilang ta a ni.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Hlauthâwng suh aw, i thil duh chu ka tihsak vek ang che. Kan khaw mipuite hian hmeichhe fel tak i nih an hria asin.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Eng pawh ni se, in laichîn bul chu ka ni ngei mai; amaherawhchu, kei aia bul zâwk a la awm.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Zânin chu hetah mu ve phawt la, naktûkah laichîn bul tih tûr a tih duh loh erawh chuan keiman ka ti ang tih Lalpa chhâlin tûnah ka tiam a che, khawvâr hma chu mu ve phawt mai rawh,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Khawvâr hma chu a ke bulah chuan a mu a, zîng takah tu ma hriat hmain a tho va; Boaza chuan, “Hruiha i lo kal hi tu man hre suh se,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Tin, a hnênah, “I puan bah lai kha han la la, dawh rawh le,” a ti a. Tichuan, a phah a, barli ṭîn khat zet a ruhsak a, puanah chuan a chhûng a, Ruthi chuan khuaah a hâwnpui ta a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />A pi hnên a han thlen chuan, “Ka fanu, eng nge i an le?” a lo ti a. Ruthi chuan a chunga Boaza thil lo tih zawng zawng chu a hrilh a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />“I pi hnênah chuan saruakin haw suh, tiin he barli ṭîn khat hi min pe a ni,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Naomi chuan, “Ka fanu, thil inher dân tûr i hriat hma chu nghâk hle hle mai rawh; thil a chin fel hma chu a ngawi mai mai dâwn si lo,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <chapter number="4" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Boaza chu rorêlna hmun kulh kawngkaah chuan a chho va, a ṭhu a. An laichîn bul, a chungchâng Boazan a sawi kha a lo kal a. Boaza chuan, “Unaupa, hetah lo kal la, ṭhu teh khai,” a ti a. A lo kal a, a ṭhu ta a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Boaza chuan chu khuaa upa sâwm a khâwm a, an hnênah, “Hetah hian ṭhu teh u khai,” a ti a, an ṭhu ta a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />An laichîn bul bera hnênah chuan, “Moab ram aṭanga lo kîr Naomi chuan kan unaupa Elimeleka ram kha hralh a duh a;
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />nang hi hrilh hmasak che ṭhain ka hria a, i tlan duh chuan hêng upaho hriatah hian tlan ta che; i tlan duh loh erawh chuan min hrilh rawh; nang lo chu tu mah tlantu tûr an awm lo; tin, kei hi i dawt chu ka ni,” a ti a. Ani chuan, “Ka tlan ang e,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Boaza chuan, “Naomi hnên aṭanga ram i lei hun chuan mitthi hming dai lova ram chanpual luahtu tûr an awm zêl theih nân Moab hmeichhia, mitthi nupui chu, i nei tel bawk tûr a ni,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />An laichînpa chuan, “Ka tân chuan ka tlan thei lo, chutilo zawng, ka roluah chungchângah harsatna ka siam dah ang e, tlantu tûr ka nihna pawh nangman chang mai la, ka tlan thei lo a ni e,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Hmânlaiin Israel-ho zîngah thil an leiin emaw, an inthlengin emaw a nemngheh nân a hralhtuin a pheikhawk a phelh a, a leitu hnênah a pe ṭhîn. Hei hi Israel-te zîngah tih ṭhin dân a ni.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />An laichînpa chuan Boaza hnênah, “I tân nangman lei mai rawh,” tiin a pheikhawk a phelh a, a pe a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Boaza chuan upaho leh mipui zawng zawng hnênah, “Vawiin hian Elimeleka thil neih zawng zawng te, Kiliona leh Mahlona thil neih zawng zawng nên Naomi hnên aṭangin ka lei ta tih hretu in ni e.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Chu bâkah, mitthi hming chu dai lova, a ro luahtu siamsak tûr leh mitthi chu a chipuite zîngah leh a awmna khaw kulh kawngkaa hriat reng a nih theih nân, Moab hmeichhia, Mahlona nupui chu, ka nupui atân ka nei ta a; tûnah, nangniho hi a hretute in ni e,” a ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Tichuan, kulh kawngkaa upaho leh mipui awm zawng zawng chuan, “Hretute kan ni e, i ina hmeichhia lo lawi chu, Israel chhûngkaw dintu pahnih Rakili leh Leaii ang khân Lalpa chuan siam rawh se. Nang pawh, he hnam zîngah hian mi ropui tak ni la, Bethlehem mi hmingthang tak ni ang che.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Lalpan he hmeichhe lakah hian fate pe che sela, i chhûngkua chu Juda-in Tamari laka fa a hrin Pereza chhûngkua ang lo ni rawh se,” an ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Boaza chuan Ruthi chu nupui atân a hruai a, an awm dûn ta a. Lalpa chuan nau a paitîr a, fapa a hring ta a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Chuta hmeichhiate chuan Naomi hnênah, “Vawiina laichîn bul chham lova awmtîrtu che Lalpa chu fakin awm rawh se; I tupa chu Israel ram pum puiah a hming lo thang sela,
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />ani chu i nun tihlimtu leh i tar châwmtu lo ni rawh se. I monu, nangmah hmangaihtu, fapa pasarih aia tama hlu zâwk chuan ani hi a hrinsak ta si che a,” an ti a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Naomi chuan nau chu a la a, a pawm a, a awm ta a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />An vênga hmeichhiate chuan a hming an sa a, “Naomi tân fapa a lo piang ta,” tiin a hmingah Obeda an sa a, chu mi chu Davida pu, Jesaia pa a ni.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Hei hi Pereza chhûngkua inthlah chhâwn dân chu a ni.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Hezrona chu Rama pa a ni, Rama chu Aminadaba pa a ni a.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Aminadaba chu Nasona pa a ni a, Nasona chu Salmona pa a ni.
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Tin, Salmona chu Boaza pa a ni a, Boaza chu Obeda pa a ni,
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Obeda chu Jesaia pa a ni a, Jesaia chu Davida pa a ni.
  </para>
</usx>
